From 4eb783b6b8fdbab4d507ba54f18293acfd6fd92a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fangzhi Zuo <jerry.zuo@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:06:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] [FROM-ML] drm/amd/display: refresh cached HDMI FreeSync
 state

When an HDMI sink re-reports an EDID without an AMD VSDB,
get_amd_vsdb() returns false but the connector's cached vsdb_info was
previously updated only on success. A previous FreeSync-capable EDID could
therefore leave freesync_supported set and keep selecting the FreeSync SPD
path instead of the HDMI VRR VTEM path.

Refresh the cached VSDB record for every HDMI EDID update so a missing AMD
VSDB clears stale FreeSync state. Keep the existing SPD/VTEM packet
separation and protocol-selection logic unchanged.

Fixes: 123e9515f7e0 ("drm/amd/display: Send HDMI VRR metadata in VTEM info packet slot")
Reviewed-by: IVAN LIPSKI <ivan.lipski@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Fangzhi Zuo <jerry.zuo@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Tom Chung <chiahsuan.chung@amd.com>
Tested-by: PeiHsin Yang <peihsiny@valvesoftware.com>
Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index dbcc0ffee62f..00debef1c069 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -4023,8 +4023,8 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 
 		if (!force_hdmi_vrr) {
 			i = parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb(amdgpu_dm_connector, edid, &vsdb_info);
+			amdgpu_dm_connector->vsdb_info = vsdb_info;
 			if (i >= 0) {
-				amdgpu_dm_connector->vsdb_info = vsdb_info;
 				sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code =
 					vsdb_info.freesync_mccs_vcp_code;
 
